>> title: Pumpkin Pie
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/pumpkin-pie-with-caramel-pecan-topping

> Note: this recipe assumes you already have @../miscellaneous/Pie Dough{}.

Preheat oven to 425 degrees F.

In a #large bowl{} beat the @eggs{2%large} and @pumpkin{15%ounce can} together. In a #medium bowl{}, combine the @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}, @ground cinnamon{1%teaspoon}, @salt{1/2%teaspoon}, @ground ginger{1/2%teaspoon} and @ground cloves{1/4%teaspoon}, and add to pumpkin mixture. 

> Note: you can also use 1 3/4 teaspoon of pumpkin pie spice in place of individual spices.

Gradually stir in the @evaporated milk{12%ounce can}. Carefully pour mixture into the @pie crust{1%9-inch}.

Bake at 425 degrees F for ~{15%minutes}. Reduce temperature to 350° F; bake for ~{40-50%minutes} longer, or until the pie is set. Check for doneness by giving the pie a gentle wiggle. The center may jiggle just a tiny bit. It will continue to set up as it cools. Or, it is done when a sharp knife inserted in center comes out clean.

Cool completely on a #wire cooling rack{}. Serve immediately with @?whipped cream{}, if desired.